; A Rust `String` coming back across the boundary.
;
; This is the shape that cannot fit contract C2 directly: it needs a
; pointer AND a length, and Axiom emits `ret i64` for every function.
; So the shim takes a trailing OUT-CELL, returns a status, and the
; ergonomic name is a GENERATED AXIOM WRAPPER that allocates the cell,
; calls `shoutRaw`, copies the bytes into a real `strAlloc` block, and
; frees the Rust side.
;
; The copy is deliberate and is the design's central safety rule: only
; Axiom's own emitter ever writes an Axiom block header, because only it
; knows MM-LIFE-2d's shape word. A Rust-authored header with a wrong
; reference bitmap does not fail loudly - it makes @axiom_release walk
; into Rust memory.
;
; `Demo.ax` is the module `axiom-bindgen` generates; the gate puts it on
; AXIOM_PATH, so this exercises the GENERATED wrapper rather than a copy
; of it written by hand.
(import IO)
(import Str)
(import Demo)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(pub fn (main)
  (let ((a (shout "hello"))
        (b (shout ""))
        (c (shout "axiom")))
    (if (&& (strEq a "HELLO!")
        (&& (strEq b "!")
            (strEq c "AXIOM!")))
        { (println "owned bytes: agree") 0 }
        { (println a) (println b) (println c) 1 })))
; expect 0
